# Section 5: the ge template — coverage by the canonical guards (T-cover)

**Generated by a program that is not included in this repository** (from a fixed text; the data and
the certificates are in `AddGECoverData.lean`).

`docs/section5/08_proof_plan.md` §7 (T-cover), §9.  For an arbitrary simple counter-clockwise
polygon `P` containing the template chain (`ChainAt P addGEV a`) whose other edges avoid `addGER`:

* the **template region** `addGETR` (a finite union of convex integer pieces) contains the filled
  region of the closed template chain `addGEK` (the chain closed by the **mouth** `addGEMouth`, the
  segment from the last chain vertex `e_j` back to the first one), `addGEK_filled_subset`; `addGEK.filled`
  is a room of `P` with the mouth as door (`addGE_room`) and `addGETR ⊆ P.filled` (`addGETR_subset`);
* **coverage** (`addGE_cover`): for guard values in `[1/2, 2]` satisfying the constraint `u_C ≤ u_A + u_B`
  (the guard of `r'_i` having the value `u` of `r_i`, exact weak copy), every point of `addGETR` is
  seen by one of the canonical guards: `addGEA u` (`r'_i`), `addGEB v` (`r_j`), `addGEC w` (`r_l`), `addGEI u`
  (`r_i`) and the stationary guard `g`.  The zone `Γ` is covered by the mechanism lemma
  `addGE_cover_Zg2` (the argument of `addGE_gamma_iff` on a possibly enlarged zone), the nook by the two-dimensional nook zone `addGECvZn2` (`CopyPair.nook_covered`);
* **the mouth** (`addGE_mouth_sees`, `addGE_sees_beyond_mouth`): the guard of `r_j` sees the mouth,
  hence every point beyond it in the angle of the mouth that is seen from the whole mouth.
-/

